<h1>Experiments</h1>
<p>
  This page exists purely to demonstrate a handful of HTML tags that don't really fit naturally into my
  portfolio content: <code>&lt;template&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audio&gt;</code>,
  <code>&lt;video&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;source&gt;</code>. It's linked
  from the footer of every page rather than the main navigation, since it's a technical demo rather than
  portfolio content.
</p>

<section id="custom-elements-demo">
  <h2>Custom Elements</h2>
  <p>
    <b>&lt;skill-tag&gt;</b> is styled with CSS only (no JavaScript). You can see it used all over
    the Projects and Home pages: <skill-tag>example-tag</skill-tag>
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>&lt;earthquake-feed&gt;</b> is the graded custom element for this assignment: a
    network-backed widget with a full idle/loading/success/error lifecycle. See it live on the
    <a href="/">home page</a>, or read the reference in the project README.
  </p>
</section>

<section id="template-demo">
  <h2>&lt;template&gt;</h2>
  <p>
    The template below defines a reusable list-item layout, reused by the earthquake widget on the
    home page. A browser skips a <code>&lt;template&gt;</code>'s contents entirely until JavaScript
    clones it, so you won't see anything printed below this paragraph, and that's expected.
  </p>
  <template id="project-card-template">
    <article class="project-card">
      <img src="" alt="">
      <h3></h3>
      <p></p>
    </article>
  </template>
</section>

